A Reminder to the Librarian.text:
{{BoH_Item
|image1=[[File:Letter.generic.png]]
|type=[[Readable]], [[Correspondence]]}}
{{Quote|A reminder from St Rhonwen's Trust that I hadn't yet replied to them.}}
<br/>'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a [[Readable]] [[Correspondence]], which the Librarian will receive every [[Season]], if they don't reply after receiving [[A Letter to the Librarian]].

===[[Consider]] this:===
{{Quote|The Letter Reads...<br/>The Trust hopes I've arrived safely, but wonders why, if so, I haven't yet replied. The letter is signed simply 'the Trustees'.}}

It is otherwise functionally identical to [[A Letter to the Librarian]].

[[Category:Readable]]
[[Category:Correspondence]]

Skills.text:
[[File:Skill.png|right]]
{{quote|Anything can be learnt; everything can be forgotten.}}{{Tocright}}
<br/>'''Skills''' are the Librarian's special abilities. Each Skill has a Primary [[Principles|Principle]] and a Secondary Principle. Skills are used for exploring the [[Wisdoms|Tree of Wisdoms]] (gaining new [[Elements of the Soul|Soul]] cards in the process), [[Elements of the Soul#Evolution|Evolving existing Soul]] cards, [[Consider|Studying]], and [[Crafting]]. There are 63 Skills, and a further 10 Languages, in Book of Hours. 

== Principles & Leveling Up ==
Each skill starts out with two of its Primary Principle and one of its Secondary Principle. Skills can be leveled up to have higher Principle values using [[Memory#Lessons|Lessons]], which can be acquired by studying books. When a skill is leveled up, each Principle is increased by one. Level 9 is the maximum level for skills. 

Upgrading a Skill requires at least one Lesson. The total number of Lessons/[[Memory|Memories]] required corresponds to the next level of the skill (ex. upgrading a skill to lvl. 2 requires one Lesson and one Memory). Lessons/Memories are referred to as Understanding, and must match at least one of the skill's Principles.

Many Skills do not have enough related books to provide 9 Lessons in total (some have only 4 or 5 e.g.). There also no dedicated Lessons for Languages. However, there are some Skills for which there is more than 9 Lessons to be found. Additionally, considering a Skill in [[Numa]] produces multiple [[A Lesson of Many Facets]] Lessons, essentially converting previously used Memories into universal Lessons (see [[Numa]] for more details). Thus, it's important to note that '''the Lesson does <u>not</u> have to be of the same Skill you are upgrading, as long as the Principles match. As a result, it's possible to get virtually all the Skills to Level 9 with enough effort.'''

== Soul Evolution ==
Evolving an [[Elements of the Soul|Element of the Soul]] requires:

* A Skill attuned to that Element (obtained through attunement in the [[The Tree of Wisdoms|Tree of Wisdoms]]).
* Two of the same Element, at the same level.
* A [[Workstations|Workstation]] matching both the Skill's [[Wisdoms|Wisdom]], and the [[Principles]] of the Skill/Element 

What is important to note, is that it's recommended to '''attune your Skill to an Element that matches (one of) its Principles.''' This makes it easier to Evolve your Soul cards, as you only need to find a Workstation that matches the shared Principle (rather than two different Principles). See the [[Elements of the Soul#Evolution|Elements of the Soul]] page for more detailed information regarding Soul Evolution.

== Crafting ==
Certain Skills can be used for Crafting. Crafting can be done at any [[Workstations|Workstation]] and has 3 challenge levels: Prentice, Scholar, and Keeper. To successfully craft something, one must use the correct skill and have a combined amount of 5 (Prentice), 10 (Scholar), or 15 (Keeper) power in one [[Principles|Principle]]. See the [[Crafting|Crafting page]] for more detailed information.

== Specialties ==
Some Skills have additional abilities, which can be used for removing [[Contamination]] from [[Readable|Books]] or for [[Crafting]]:
