== Languages ==
[[File:Skill.language.png|right]]
{{Quote|A skill that can be used to read particular books, among other much less important things.}}
<br/>'''Languages''' are almost identical to regular Skills, with a couple exceptions:

* They are acquired through paying [[Visitors]] for a tutoring lesson.
* Relevant [[Memory|Lessons]] can only be randomly obtained at the [[Salon|Salons]].
* Most importantly, they must be used as an 'extra' skill when reading [[Readable|Books]] written in Languages that the Librarian does not know by default.

As one only needs to use (a minimum of) one Lesson with matching [[Principles]] to upgrade a Skill, Languages can still be upgraded even with different Lessons. Furthermore, Languages (just like regular skills) can be committed to the [[The Tree of Wisdoms|Tree of Wisdoms]].

=== Acquiring a Language ===
Languages can be learnt from the random Visitors that appear each [[Season]] (including [[Numa]]) or can be invited to the Hush House. Instead of speaking to them about any active event cards, the Librarian must "hire" them as a tutor, similar to hiring assistance from [[The Sweet Bones]]. Visitors must be paid an [[Tally|Iron Spintria]] instead of regular currency. Doing so will begin a 3 minute timer, at the end of which the visitor will leave, even if they came for an active event. It's also possible to get a Lesson by inviting the Visitor who knows this Language to the Salon and make them engage in the conversation with other Visitors, however, this method is random and not reliable.

