Loom.text:
{{Workstation
|image1=[[File:Loom.png]]
|principles={{Lore|Heart}}, {{Lore|Moth}}, {{Lore|Nectar}}, {{Lore|Rose}}
|location=[[Servants' Hall]]
|fourth_slot_aspects=[[Fabric and Fibre]]
|fifth_slot_aspects=[[Fabric and Fibre]]}}
{{quote|And there the golden threads they wove - and in the Moon's House, fast they tied them.|From the Lay of Helgi Hundingsbane}}
<br/>The '''Loom''' is a [[Workstation]] located in the [[Servants' Hall]]. Its Principles are {{Lore|Heart}}, {{Lore|Moth}}, {{Lore|Nectar}}, {{Lore|Rose}}. 

It is the only Workstation that can take [[Fabric and Fibre]], making it one of few Workstations that ''can'' make a [[Pale Mommet]] - however, it does not take {{Lore|Grail}}, so the only way to [[Crafting|Craft]] a Pale Mommet here is to use a combination [[Resurgences & Emergences]], [[Chor]], [[Bolt of Moss-Green Velvet]] or [[Warmly Coloured Yarns]], and a [[Memory]] such as [[Memory: Satisfaction|Satisfaction]] to reach the 10 {{Lore|Grail}} needed; it may be more straightforward to use [[Rags]] or [[Human Hair]] (if you can obtain some) to craft Pale Mommet at a Workstation that takes [[Fuel]] or [[Remains]], respectively.

[[Category:Workstation]]

