A Lesson of Many Facets.text:
{{BoH Memory
|title=A Lesson of Many Facets
|principles={{Lore|Sky}}, {{Lore|Winter}}, {{Lore|Lantern}}, {{Lore|Edge}}, {{Lore|Forge}}, {{Lore|Scale}}, {{Lore|Heart}}, {{Lore|Grail}}, {{Lore|Rose}}, {{Lore|Knock}}, {{Lore|Nectar}}, {{Lore|Moth}}, {{Lore|Moon}}
|aspects=[[Memory]], [[Memory#Lessons|Lesson]]
|image=File:A_Lesson_of_Many_Facets.PNG
|obtained_by=[[Consider]]ing a [[Skill]] in [[Numa]]
}}
{{Quote|Light leaks in where, from, how. [An unusual and versatile lesson that will NOT PERSIST PAST DAWN. Use it quickly.]}}

''{{PAGENAME}}'' is a [[Memory]] that can be acquired in [[Numa]] by [[consider|breaking down]] an uncommitted [[skill]]. Doing so returns the total number of memories spent on the skill that was broken down, -1, of this lesson. The benefit of this is that it is a universal lesson, having one of each [[Principles|principle]], so if the Librarian is prepared with memories and [[Elements of the Soul]], they can quickly level up skills during Numa. A more in-depth guide to using this lesson can be found [[Numa|here]]. Like all other memories, {{PAGENAME}} will disappear at dawn, so it is recommended to plan ahead before breaking any skills down.

[[Category:Memory]]

Avenue of Enquiry.text:
{{BoH Memory
|image=[[File:Avenue of Enquiry.png]]
|principles={{Lore|Edge|1}}, {{Lore|Forge|1}}, {{Lore|Heart|1}}, {{Lore|Moon|1}}, {{Lore|Moth|1}}, {{Lore|Rose|1}}
|aspects=[[Memory]], [[Persistent]]
}}
{{Quote|A recourse that a wise Librarian might employ only as a versatile memory. There is an alternative. [Great Ink of Power; handy Soul element; incaution; readiness; blank writing medium; Inquiry via this Avenue. Wise? Absence is true skill.]}}

An '''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a [[Persistent]] [[Memory]], which can be created by combining two [[Inkling]]s.

It can be used by the Librarian at a [[Workstations#Desks|Desk]] with a compatible [[Element of the Soul]], [[Blank]] paper (or even the [[Writing-Case]]) and an [[Encaustum Terminale]] in order to meddle with events, forcefully creating a new [[Incident]] if any still remain undrawn. This action will take 10 seconds and will not destroy the paper used.

{{Quote|It is not the Librarian's business to meddle in the world beyond Hush House. But sometimes the Librarian gets curious; sometimes the Librarian misuses their prerogatives because they grow restless. [This will precipitate an Incident, if any yet remain undrawn. If there's already an Incident, Visitors might not initially interact with the one you intend. Instigate informedly, Ys-incipient.]}}

[[Category:Memory]]
[[Category:Persistent]]
[[Category:Incident]]
[[Category:Further Stories]]

An Offering to St Tentreto.text:
{{Stub}}
{{BoH Memory
|image=[[File:An Offering to St Tentreto.png]]
|aspects=[[Memory]], [[Liquid]]}}
{{Quote|Heart-coloured liquid sloshes inside a fragile exoskeletal remnant. Hold it carefully.}}
<br/>{{PAGENAME}} is a [[Memory]] and [[Liquid]], which is received as a part of a [[Further Stories|Further Story]] involving [[Mr Ehsan Fekri]] and [[Mr Peter Agdistis]], after completing [[The Affair of the Claw and the Clouds]].

If the offering is taken to the [[Altar: St Tentreto]] and used in its '''Devotion''' or '''Remembrance''' slots, it will permanently allow using {{Lore|Heart}} there and provides {{Lore|Heart|2}} innately.

{{Quote|St Tentreto has four wings. So I should pour the offering into his four fires. That seems self-evident, now that I'm here.<br/><br/>Once the walkers and fliers and swimmers and fire-seekers gave a little of their blood to the West, every sunset, and the Sun's night-self protected them until the dawn. Now blood has been sent from the West to the isle's heart. What does that mean? Not eternity; a change. [The altar now admits Heart intention, and provides Heart aspect.]}}

<br/>After that, it becomes a [[Remnant of an Offering to St Tentreto]], which can be returned to [[Mr Ehsan Fekri]] or [[Mr Peter Agdistis]].

While An Offering to St Tentreto has the Memory Aspect, it does not disappear at dawn, despite not having the Persistent aspect. It has not yet been tested as to whether the offering or the remnant will disappear at the end of Numa, however.

[[Category:Memory]]
[[Category:Liquid]]
[[Category:Further Stories]]

