The Midwife.text:
{{PersonInfobox
|title1=Mrs Kille
|image1=The_Midwife.png
|principles={{Lore|Grail|2}}, {{Lore|Heart|1}}
|aspects=[[Assistance]], [[An Introduction]]
|fee=12p}}
{{Quote|As somber as autumn, as kind as autumn. She also likes her beer.}}
__NOTOC__<br/>'''Mrs Kille''' is an inhabitant of [[Brancrug Village]], and the [[Librarians|Librarian's]] acquaintance if [[Ereb]] is chosen in [[The Beginning]].

For a [[Pence#Denominations|Shilling]] (or free if she is your acquaintance), Mrs Kille can be hired as an [[Assistants|Assistant]]. Her [[Principles]] are {{Lore|Grail|2}} and {{Lore|Heart|1}}. Unlike other Assistants, Mrs Kille can make use of [[Fabric]].

If Mrs Kille is your acquaintance, you can also hire her husband, [[The Coffinmaker|Mr Kille]], free of charge.

In the ''[[House of Light]]'' DLC, she and her husband can be invited to a [[Salon]] once per [[Season]]. Their card will remain in the Sundries tab until used for a Salon, but they can still be hired and used to unlock rooms as usual.

==Introduction==
===An Old Friend's Address===
{{quote|Mrs Kille is the handywoman - the midwife - of Brancrug village. I knew her long ago in Paris, when her surname was not 'Kille' but 'Raveline', and her sister was a viscountess. Her home is always open to me (though she's asked me not to bring up the title thing when Mr Kille's around). I can find shelter for tonight under their roof - <b>once I've reached Brancrug Village</b>.}}
<br/>If Mrs Kille is the Librarian's acquaintance, she will provide shelter and warmth following the storm, and she and her husband will always offer their services for free. 

{{Quote|Mrs Kille opens the door with caution, but flings it wide, letting the wind bang it, when she sees me.<br/><br/>'Mrs Kille drags me into her broad embrace, releases me when she realises how damp I am, and then she's calling for Mr Kille and dragging me into the warmth of the parlour. 'Sit 'ee down and get a drop of warm in!', she enjoins sternly.<br/><br/>Mr K constructed the bed himself - I rather fear with the same tools he uses to shape coffins. It is not a comfortable bed. But it's dry, clean, and warm.<br/><br/>Mrs K and I sit up late talking over old times in the Latin Quarter, when the world and we were very different. Mr K listens as he cleans his pipe. 'Wine and roses,' he observes. 'Spose the wine is all spilt now, but the roses'll come up again, won't them?'}}

==Mrs and Mr Kille [Locked]==
{{quote|Mrs Kille the midwife is tall and gloomy. Mr Kille the undertaker is slight and wry. In these troubled times, both are wary of strangers.}}
Unlocking Mrs and Mr Kille's requires [[An Introduction]] with {{Lore|Winter}}, {{Lore|Grail}}, {{Lore|Heart}}, {{Lore|Sky}}, {{Lore|Lantern}} or {{Lore|Moon}}.

After unlocking Mrs and Mr Kille's, both Killes can be hired as [[Assistants]].

==Conversation==
{{quote|Mrs Kille has seen more of the world than she usually lets on. Conversations with her yield the occasional surprise.}}
[[Talk]]ing with Mrs Kille will draw one of the following [[Memory|Memories]] at random:
{{#lst:Decks|d.chat.traveller}}
==Salon==
She and her husband can be invited to a Salon by using the [[Writing-Case]] in the ''Topic'' verb. They will gift the Librarian one of the following items:
{{Quote|Mr Kille is clearly excited, and remains courteous. Mrs Kille is courteous, and may be excited: as ever, it's difficult to tell. [The Killes have sent a gift ahead.]}}
{{#lst:Decks|killes.invite}}

=== Hidden Interactions ===
{{Spoilers
| content = <br/>A special interaction happens every time you place a glass of [[Domaine Raveline]] on an eligible [[Salon]] attended by Mrs Kille.<br/>

If you present an [[Ereb]] card, the Librarian is awarded with a [[Stone Stories|Lesson: Stone Stories]] and the following dialogue:
{{Quote|<nowiki/>With clear caution, Mrs Kille samples the wine - red wine from the bottle with the Domaine Raveline label. As the taste crosses her tongue, her usual melancholy melts, and she smiles; but then she locks the smile away. 'I left all that behind,' she says. Her Cornish accent has blurred, like tempera in rain, so that another accent beneath it has become visible - something no warmer, but more quicksilver. 'I left all that behind before the qualities in the soil could enter my bones. Though all of us carry a little of it. And so I will never have children of my own. You understand, my darling' - she is speaking to Mr Kille - 'you understand, don't you? And you understand that I will take the small risk' - still to Mr Kille - 'of finishing this glass.'}}
| caption = This section contains information on hidden interactions.
}}
