The Coffinmaker.text:
{{PersonInfobox
|title1=Mr Kille
|aspects=[[Assistance]], [[An Introduction]]
|image1=File:The_Coffinmaker.png
|fee=12p
|principles={{Lore|Sky|1}}, {{Lore|Winter|2}}}}
{{Quote|A tamer of trees, a worker of woods, a consigner of cadavers. He has also been known to try his hand, very diffidently, at poetry.<br/> [Make use of the Coffinmaker's help before dawn.]}}
__NOTOC__<br/>'''Mr Kille''' is an inhabitant of [[Brancrug Village]], and the [[Librarians|Librarian's]] acquaintance if [[Wist]] is chosen in [[The Beginning]].

For a [[Pence#Denominations|Shilling]] (or free if he is your acquaintance), Mr Kille can be hired as an [[Assistants|Assistant]]. His [[Principles]] are {{Lore|Sky|1}} and {{Lore|Winter|2}}. Unlike other Assistants, Mr Kille can make use of [[Wood]].

If Mr Kille is your acquaintance, you can also hire his wife, [[The Midwife|Mrs Kille]], free of charge.

In the ''[[House of Light]]'' DLC, he and his wife can be invited to a [[Salon]] once per [[Season]]. Their card will remain in the Sundries tab until used for a Salon, but they can still be hired and used to unlock rooms as usual.

==Introduction==
===An Old Friend's Address===
{{quote|Mr Kille is the coffinmaker of Brancrug Village. I once wrote kindly of his poetry. His home is always open to me (though he's asked me never to mention poetry in front of Mrs Kille). I can find shelter for tonight under their roof - <b>once I've reached Brancrug Village</b>. }}
<br/>If Mr Kille is the Librarian's acquaintance, he will provide shelter and warmth following the storm, and he and his wife will always offer their services for free.

{{Quote|Mr Kille struggles with the door. The wind almost snatches it from his hands. His eyes widen as he sees me.<br/><br/>Mr Kille is grinning like the happiest of skulls. 'Come in, come in! Less 'ee wants fitted for a box?' And he leads me into the warmth of the parlour, calling for Mrs Kille to come see, come see the rescue.<br/><br/>Mr Kille constructed the bed himself - I rather fear with the same tools he uses to shape coffins. It is not a comfortable bed. But it's dry, clean, and warm.<br/><br/>I sit up talking with Mr and Mrs K, as the wind rattles the shutters and the fire shrugs its way emberward. I'm very hungry, and Mrs K's galettes are impossibly good. Mr K pretends to grumble about foreign cooking. No-one is convinced.}}

==Mrs and Mr Kille [Locked]==
{{quote|Mrs Kille the midwife is tall and gloomy. Mr Kille the undertaker is slight and wry. In these troubled times, both are wary of strangers.}}
Unlocking [[Mrs and Mr Kille]] requires [[An Introduction]] with {{Lore|Winter}}, {{Lore|Grail}}, {{Lore|Heart}}, {{Lore|Sky}}, {{Lore|Lantern}} or {{Lore|Moon}}.

After unlocking Mrs and Mr Kille's, both Killes can be hired as [[Assistants]].

==Conversation==
{{quote|Mr Kille, wry and spry, doesn't mind stopping for a gossip.}}
[[Talk]]ing with Mr Kille will draw one of the following [[Memory|Memories]] at random:
